One other idea, in case it might be of some use: Have you checked
whether the SRM upgrade switched the 'console' variable to
'serial'?  On a recent UP2000 SRM upgrade I did, I ended up with
'console=serial' and/or 'ostype=nt'.  Even after getting the
console set to graphics, the ostype variable handed control to
AlphaBIOS, which couldn't handle the graphics card I had in the
machine at the time.  If your situation is similar, one solution
would be to use the serial console to set the variables.  Another
solution would be to put in a very basic graphics card that any
SRM/AlphaBIOS will talk to, at least until you get the variables
set correctly.

Good luck.

