Let's face it - ext3 in not yet as stable as ext2. I have had some
serious fs corruptions with ext3 some of which are for no apparent
reason, others following a brown-out (sudden reboot).

You mention that you are using it for Samba shares - Did you add
extended attributes and access control list to the kernel ? If so
you should revert to ext2, and perhaps consider using LVM to create
smaller volumes - If you really need a journaling fs but do not need
acl, why not try Reiser ? From what I have seen Reiser is stable
at least compared to ext3 ....


